<title>GERMANY: German DBAG plans 3-for-1 capital rise.</title>
<headline>German DBAG plans 3-for-1 capital rise.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>German investment group Deutsche Beteiligungs AG said on Tuesday it planned to raise its nominal capital in the ratio three for one to 60 million marks from 15 million.</p>
<p>In a mandatory statement, DBAG said it was taking advantage of shareholders' approval for a capital increase. Its supervisory board had approved the move.</p>
<p>More details would be made available before the mid-April to early May period when the increase was expected to take place.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
